<title>USA: Santander sells preference shares.</title>
<headline>Santander sells preference shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Santander SA said its subsidiary Santander Finance Ltd Tuesday placed $200 million in non-cumulative guaranteed preference shares, with a par value of $25 each.</p>
<p>The Series E share issue carries a cash dividend of 8.54 percent, payable quarterly in arrears in U.S. dollars starting September 30, 1996, the bank said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
